WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Maya Lopez: Morning everyone. Three things today: the DataStore saving outage from Tuesday, the rare pet balance complaints, and whether we still ship the hatching update on Saturday.

2
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Jordan Lee: Okay, the outage first. On Tuesday about four hundred players lost progress because our saves were being throttled. We were writing the whole profile every ten seconds.

3
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Maya Lopez: Every ten seconds? I thought autosave ran once a minute.

4
00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Jordan Lee: It was supposed to, but the pet inventory change added a second save loop. Both loops hit the DataStore, so we blew through the request budget during peak hours.

5
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Sam Park: Did we lose anything permanently, or can the profiles be restored?

6
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Jordan Lee: Most of it is recoverable from the version history. I restored about three hundred profiles already. The rest need the backup script.

7
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Maya Lopez: Good. What stops this from happening again?

8
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Jordan Lee: I'd remove the second loop and add session locking, so two servers can never write the same profile. I'll have the session locking done by Thursday.

9
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:06.000
Lee Chen: Should we also add an alert when the save queue backs up? We would have caught this in minutes instead of hours.

10
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Maya Lopez: Yes, let's add the alert. Lee, can you set that up this week?

11
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Lee Chen: Sure, I'll wire it into the dashboard by Wednesday.

12
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Sam Park: And the players who lost progress, do we compensate them?

13
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:33.000
Maya Lopez: We decided to give every affected player a free rare egg. Sam, can you write the announcement?

14
00:02:33.000 --> 00:03:02.000
Sam Park: Yes, I'll post it on the forum tomorrow.

15
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:15.000
Sam Park: Next topic, the rare pet balance. The forum is full of complaints that players hatch a hundred eggs and never see a rare pet.

16
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:33.000
Lee Chen: The rare rate is one in fifty right now, but with bad luck streaks some players go two hundred hatches without one. The average looks fine, the worst cases feel terrible.

17
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:38.000
Maya Lopez: What would fix the worst cases without making rares common?

18
00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:55.000
Lee Chen: A pity counter. Every hatch without a rare raises the chance a little, and after forty hatches a rare is guaranteed. Most games in the genre do this now.

19
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:06.000
Jordan Lee: The counter has to be saved in the profile, otherwise players reset it by rejoining. That touches the same save code we just talked about.

20
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:14.000
Maya Lopez: Then the pity counter waits until session locking is in. Lee, can you model the numbers for a guarantee at forty versus fifty hatches?

21
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:20.000
Lee Chen: Will do, I'll bring a spreadsheet to Tuesday's meeting.

22
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:28.000
Sam Park: Do rare pets keep their stats after trading? A lot of the complaints are about traded pets losing their bonuses.

23
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:36.000
Jordan Lee: Good question, I don't actually know. Trading was written before the stats system.

24
00:04:36.000 --> 00:05:10.000
Maya Lopez: Let's find out before we change anything else in trading.

25
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:16.000
Maya Lopez: Last topic, the hatching update release. Are we still on for Saturday?

26
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:28.000
Jordan Lee: The update itself is ready. The risk is the trading exploit: players can duplicate rare pets if they trade during a server shutdown.

27
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:31.000
Sam Park: How long would a fix take?

28
00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:44.000
Jordan Lee: About two days. The fix is to lock both profiles while the trade saves, which is the same session locking work.

29
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:52.000
Maya Lopez: So if session locking lands Thursday, the exploit is fixed too, and we can still ship Saturday.

30
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:58.000
Lee Chen: I'd still disable trading for the first day after the update, just to be safe.

31
00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:10.000
Maya Lopez: Agreed. We'll ship the hatching update on Saturday with trading turned off for the first twenty four hours. I'll write the patch notes.

32
00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:15.000
Sam Park: I'll schedule the release post for Saturday morning.

33
00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:20.000
Maya Lopez: Great, thanks everyone.
